  "text": "BentoPDF\nBack to Tools\nBentoPDF›Add Page Labels\nAdd Page Labels\n\nApply PDF page labels with Roman numerals, prefixes, and custom starts.\n\nClick to select a file or drag and drop\n\nPDF file\n\nYour files never leave your device.\n\nreport.pdf\n3.7 KB • 4 pages\nHow labels work\nLeave Page Range empty to label all pages.\nUse styles like Roman numerals for front matter and decimal numbering for the main body.\nUse Prefix with Start Value 0 to create labels such as A-0, A-1, A-2.\nEnable progress when one rule uses a disjoint range such as 1-9,30-40 or odd.\nLabel Rules\nAdd Rule\nLabel Rule 1\nPage Range\nLabel Style\nDecimal Arabic\nLowercase Roman\nUppercase Roman\nLowercase Letters\nUppercase Letters\nNo Label Prefix Only\nLabel Prefix\nStart Value\nContinue numbering across disjoint ranges\n\nExamples: 1-4 for Roman front matter, 15-20 with prefix A- and start value 0, or odd with progress enabled.\n\nRemove existing page labels before applying these rules\n\nThis tool uses CoherentPDF in your browser. If CoherentPDF is not configured, you will be prompted to set it up in WASM Settings.\n\nAdd Page Labels\nSuccess\n\nPage labels added successfully!\n\nOK\nBentoPDF\n\n© 2026 BentoPDF. All rights reserved.\n\nVersion 2.8.10\n\nEnglish",
